Every kind accepts an optional
.Va comment ,
a note for whoever reads the specification.
Intervals are written as one or more
.Ql <number> <unit>
pairs \(em year, month, week, day, hour, minute, second \(em and sent to
PostgreSQL as written.
They are compared as PostgreSQL keeps them, as months, days and seconds, so
.Ql 1 week
and
.Ql 7 days
are the same and
.Ql 7 days
and
.Ql 168 hours
are not.
